* OFTPPTN0 - OFTPD partners
*
* PARTNER=name opens an entry (1..8 characters, the name commands use);
* the keywords after it belong to that partner. An entry with an error
* is disabled, the others still work.
*
* ODETTEID     the partner's Odette ID (required)
* PASSWORD     the password the partner sends
* OURPASSWORD  the password we send
* OURID        our Odette ID towards it      (ODETTEID of OFTPPRM0)
* HOST, PORT   where to call it; no HOST: never called      (-, 3305)
* LEVEL        highest OFTP level: 5 (2.0), 4 (1.4), 2 (1.3)  (5)
* SDEB, CREDIT caps for this partner               (from OFTPPRM0)
* MODE         S send only, R receive only, B both            (B)
* COMPRESS     Y: offer buffer compression                    (N)
* CALL         N: never call it, only answer                  (Y)
* ADDRESS      calls from it must come from this IP address    (-)
* XLATE        Y: translate F, V and U data EBCDIC<->ASCII     (N)
* ENABLED      N: refuse it and never call it                 (Y)
*
PARTNER=PARTNER1 ODETTEID=O0000000000PARTNER1
  PASSWORD=SECRET1 OURPASSWORD=SECRET2
  HOST=partner1.example.org PORT=3305 LEVEL=5
